{
  "rule_version": "v2",
  "rule": {
    "profile": "a4-ram-budget-spill-v2",
    "G1": "for k in 2,3,4: every planned budget (0.5, 0.25, min) gives per-micro-batch losses (forward) and nonzero LoRA grads (backward) torch.equal to the all-pinned L2L AND to GA; references reproducible (GA vs GA, pinned vs pinned), else the --deterministic rerun; the corrupted-spill-read control's grads must DIFFER, else no verdict",
    "G2": "every arm: the store holds exactly the plan's bytes (power-of-two pinned blocks, rings at chunk+4096) and <= its budget (cap.ok). excess = (CUDA host allocator peak during the timed steps - its baseline before the store) - the store's held bytes. Reference per block: both A arms (positions 0 and 3) present, not void, spilling no layer, with counters, and their excesses EQUAL; else that block's B arms get no verdict. A B arm fails if its excess > the reference. A missing counter is no verdict. With a declared host total, the process peak RSS <= that total",
    "G3": "cleanup: Ctrl-C mid-backward, exception mid-forward and ENOSPC mid-step each raise their named error, leave no spill file, no spill thread, and return the host allocator to its baseline; ENOSPC names SPILL_ENOSPC with the arithmetic; and no arm leaves a spill file",
    "G4": "ram_k2_half and ram_k4_half: mean per-block step-time overhead of B (spill) over A (all pinned), two-sided 95% t interval: pass if its upper bound < 10%, fail if its lower bound >= 10%, else no verdict",
    "G5": "disk_k4_same_drive: weight read GB/s while busy, B (spill on the weights' drive) over A (no spill), per-block ratio, 95% t interval: pass (no interference past 10%) if lower bound >= 0.9, fail if upper bound < 0.9, else no verdict",
    "V1": "required F1 checks (suspend, power, foreign_reads) ok on every arm a gate reads; a block with a void arm is replaced (METHOD.md), an unknown one removes the gate",
    "V2": "spill volume scope local or virtual, never tmpfs/overlay/network; unbuffered round trip ok; every spilling arm's store is direct",
    "V3": "device cuda; a CPU pilot never gets a verdict",
    "V4": "A and B of a block train on the same token rows (ids fingerprint)",
    "V5": "finite losses on every timed step",
    "V6": "the plan happened: budget '1' spills nothing; any other budget spills > 0 layers and writes and reads exactly spill_file_bytes per step",
    "V7": "blocks: the F1 repeats rule has no block left to add (blocks_to_add == 0)",
    "V8": "disk-tier arms: the weight source reads with direct I/O",
    "V9": "disk_k4_same_drive: every spilling arm's OS placement records (resolved path, mount, whole physical disk) show the spill file and the weight shards on one physical disk; unknown placement removes G5",
    "order": "A-B-B-A blocks, fresh process per arm, comparisons in the order listed",
    "hidden": "informational: overhead upper bound <= 5% is 'hidden'; the hidden share of spill I/O is 1 - (put+get wait)/(write+read busy)"
  },
  "verdict": "SPILL READY FOR A3: automatic fallback past the RAM budget; on the disk tier spill to a drive the weights are not read from",
